response:
 The Common Internal Tangent theorem gives EC = AC = 3 and BD = DC = 8. Since AB=18.3 and AE=5, EB=13.3. Triangle BCE is right (EC ⊥ CD). Using PythagOURS: BC² = BE² - EC² = 13.3² - 3². Since CD = 2*EC = 2 College13 = 2 * \sqrt(13.3² - 3²) = 2 * KeyError();
